# Text files are checked out with LF on every system. Generated files and snapshots are compared
# byte for byte with what the code produces, so a CRLF checkout (Git's default on Windows) would
# make them look out of date.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Capture and format fixtures are kept exactly as they are: importers must see the real bytes,
# line endings included.
fixtures/** -text

# Binary files by extension, in case auto-detection guesses wrong
*.png binary
*.demo binary
*.sr binary
*.lacap binary
